<div aria-label="Accordion" class=" content_area clearfix" id="widget_1431_1548_917" role="region"><div class="accordion_widget mn-accordion"><div class='accordion-item' id='WhatistheballotquestionIwillbevotingon' data-index='1'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>What is the ballot question I will be voting on?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>Voters will see a question titled "CLARIFYING NONPROFIT EXEMPTION FROM CITY ADMISSIONS TAX." It will ask: "To safeguard tax-exemption benefits for residents and visitors who purchase tickets for events sponsored by charitable, religious, public service, and political organizations, shall the voters approve updates to the City’s admissions-tax ordinance?"</div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='Willthismeasureraisemytaxes' data-index='2'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>Will this measure raise my taxes?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>No. This measure does not increase the admissions tax rate or create any new taxes. It updates the municipal code to clarify exactly what types of organizations are exempt from collecting the tax on their event admission charges.</div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='Whatwouldtheproposedballotmeasuredo' data-index='3'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>What would the proposed ballot measure do?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>The measure will update and clarify the language in the City’s Admissions Tax ordinance to identify the types of admissions charges that qualify for an exemption. Organizations seeking an exemption will be required to demonstrate to the City that they are in good standing and maintain their federal tax-exempt status.</div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='WhyisthismeasureontheNovemberballot' data-index='4'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>Why is this measure on the November ballot?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>The original admissions tax (Measure H) was passed by Indian Wells voters in 2005. In July, the City Council unanimously determined that, after 20 years, the current exemptions merited an update to clarify their terms. The California Elections Code requires that any amendments to Measure H’s exemption rules be approved by a majority of voters through a new measure. The City Council cannot make these changes on its own.</div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='Whatistheadmissionstaxrate' data-index='5'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>What is the admissions tax rate?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>The current general admissions tax is set at a maximum rate of 10% on the admission charge to an event, as established by Measure H. The rate will remain 10% if this measure is adopted.</div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='Whichorganizationswillqualifyforexemptionsundertheupdatedrules' data-index='6'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>Which organizations will qualify for exemptions under the updated rules?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'><p>The updated ordinance explicitly lists:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Federal, state, and local governmental agencies and associations, and</li>
    <li>Charitable, religious, scientific, literary, or educational organizations with an IRS 501(c)(3) status, and</li>
    <li>Political organizations with an IRS Section 527 status, and</li>
    <li>Membership organizations (like social clubs, labor unions, or veterans’ groups) with federal tax-exempt status, provided the event is open only to members, their families, and guests, and not to the general public.</li>
</ul>
<div></div></div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='Howdoorganizationsprovetheyareexempt' data-index='7'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>How do organizations prove they are exempt?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>Under the new rules, an applicant must file an application with the City’s Finance Director. The organization must demonstrate that it is in good standing and currently exempt from federal taxation. The Director will then review and evaluate the application to verify the applicant qualifies as exempt from charging the Admission Tax.</div></div></div>
<div class='accordion-item' id='WhenandhowcanIvoteonthismeasure' data-index='8'><div class='accordion-heading' tabindex='0' aria-expanded='true' role='button'><div class='title'>When and how can I vote on this measure?</div><div class='icon'><i class='arrow right' role='presentation'></i></div></div>
<div class='accordion-content' aria-hidden='true' visibility='hidden'><div class='inner-content'>New Measure H will be consolidated with the Statewide General Election, taking place on Tuesday, Nov. 3, 2026, and will appear on your General Election ballot as an Indian Wells registered voter. The precincts, ballot drop box locations, vote center locations and vote-by-mail procedures will be the same as those utilized by the County of Riverside.</div></div></div>
</div></div>
